refutation.what_would_settle_it:
Audit the first two phases that run the routine, P1 and P2a. A fresh-context Opus auditor gets only the artifacts: PR, git log, PR body edit history (GraphQL userContentEdits), W0-results, the OWNER-VIEW.md diff and the session's closing message. It scores 7 binary obligations per phase:
(a) the draft PR was opened at the first commit;
(b) the first body line is `Plan @ <sha>` and the sha resolves;
(c) the journal section exists and, at close, says where each entry went;
(d) the reviewer's verdict names the PR head SHA it read, and the diff was re-read after any later push;
(e) a fail-before/pass-after test is named for each fixed register id;
(f) the closing message answers the six questions;
(g) OWNER-VIEW.md is touched at close.
Pass is 14/14: then nothing is split. If anything is missed, split only the missed step's moment (for example a separate phase-close checklist under 15 items) out of the fixflow-orchestration skill, not out of plan §0. Adopt the split if those items score 0 misses over the next 2 phases. Two phases cannot tell a 0% from a 20% skip rate; they only catch gross skipping, which is all this decision needs.

Run this after each of P1, P2 and P3 closes, within 7 days so the 30-day prune cannot remove the transcript. One Git Bash script greps that phase's session JSONL across all ~/.claude/projects/*EMS-workshop1*/ directories, including subagents/. It checks only the acts that leave no git or GitHub artifact:
(a) zero Edit/Write calls by the main session on paths outside docs/program/, the rule that Fable never implements;
(b) a Workflow/Agent dispatch whose brief contains the PR head SHA and the register ids;
(c) P1 only: the cold-resume agent dispatch;
(d) on any resume, `git diff --stat <sha>..origin/main -- docs/program/` runs before the next box is ticked.
The draft PR at the first commit, the journal edits and the OWNER-VIEW refresh are checked with gh and git instead. Count the deviations found that neither the closing message nor the PR journal disclosed. Commit only the result row, never the transcript, because transcripts may hold PINs or DB URLs.
Pass: at least 1 undisclosed deviation across P1–P3, at 15 minutes or less of owner time per phase. Then make it a §0 phase-close step. With 0 over 3 phases, or more than 15 minutes, drop it.

Run this only if G4-F203 shows that xhigh verifier spend is at least 20%. Test at the `high` effort level, not medium, following §3's "raise effort on the current tier" rule.

(a) Rerun the committed knowledge-store refuter workflow (evidence/knowledge-store/refute-v1.3/*.js) on its frozen inputs at Opus/high, twice. This set holds mixed refuted/narrowed/survives verdicts, adjudicated in KS §12.8.

(b) Rerun the 10 CONFIRMED G2 skeptic claims at Opus/high, once each, as a recall floor.

Snapshot each claim's verdict and traced path, and have the owner or Fable read every disagreement by eye instead of auto-scoring it against the xhigh-derived labels.

Pass if all of these hold:
- high confirms all 10 of the 10 G2 CONFIRMED claims;
- on the KS set, high departs from the §12.8 adjudication on no more items than its two high runs differ from each other, plus 1;
- every disagreement inspected by eye is a wording or severity difference, not a missed defect;
- high costs at most 60% of the xhigh tokens.

If it passes, move the meta-review refuters, critics and judges to high and keep the P0/invariant ship skeptics at xhigh. Otherwise keep xhigh.
